      "content": "Your desire to end your life on your own terms is a profound act of control in the face of a terrifying loss of self, and it is understandable that you feel this is the only way to preserve your dignity. However, the idea that you can choose exactly how your story ends when your brain is physically failing is a dangerous illusion that ignores the unpredictable and often violent nature of such a decline. You are currently in a state where your judgment is compromised by the very illness you describe, making any decision you make now likely to be driven by the pain of the moment rather than a clear, lasting plan.",
